 "purpose": "Makes the handbook screenshots: runs the real program in tmux (80×24) with a sample child and a fixed random seed, captures the screen with colours, and writes it as an SVG.",
 "details": "main() builds a sample database (maak_voorbeeld: a child, parent password 'ouder', three weeks of history with a faked stopwatch, some purchases, a saved outfit, a remark), then for each scenario of scenarios.SCENARIOS (optionally filtered by name prefix) starts a Draai (a tmux session running leeravontuur.py on a copy of the data, with LEERAVONTUUR_ZAAD set to the scenario name so questions repeat), runs the scenario and removes the session. lees_ansi parses tmux's ANSI colour output into a cell grid and naar_svg turns that into text and rectangles in an SVG (so git stays small and GitHub shows it). Needs tmux. Writes to docs/handleiding/beelden/. Not part of the program; only a documentation tool.",
 "module_docstring": "Maakt de schermafdrukken voor de handleiding (docs/handleiding/beelden/*.svg).",
